Hi, this is Caitlin Luna, host of Speaking of Psychology. This podcast was recorded live during the 2018 APA convention in San Francisco. This episode is about how our memories may not be as reliable as we'd like to think. As always, we want to hear from you, so please email me at K-Luna at APA.org. If you have any comments or ideas for us, that's K-L-U-N-A-A-A-D-Rg. I'm joined by Dr. Elizabeth Loftus, a distinguished professor of the University of California, Vine. Dr. Loftus is well known for her research on human memory, notably false memories. Dr. Loftus has been honored by APA's review of general psychology as one of the 100 most eminent

